Keep wishes for after Soko, you *do* want MR, reflection and drain  
resistances asap (especially the first two). Since Soko can provide  
reflection or not, keep a wish for after that.

If you need a BoH after Soko, wish for the wallet of Perseus, it's better.
Don't bother with magic whistle, enhanced helmet or enhanced gauntlet,  
you'll upgrade some of the mundane items with potions of gain level to get  
them.

Oh, and Whisperfeet are better than standard speed boots (buth they're  
neutral) (provide stealth, iirc, plus since artefact should resist  
curse/desintegration (?))

Magic markers never were a problem for me in slash'em (ascended once,  
reached Gehennom two other times). You usually find enough of them or  
unihorn to polypile. Plus many many scrolls, too.

Spellbooks of identify were never a problem for me in nethack or slash'em.  
I think I used the spell in only one game. I will certainly rather burn a  
wish on charm monster rather than indentify if I go for spellbook.

Rings of regen is not that useful in slash'em, you'll find Vecna's hand  
more convenient even if harder to get at.

Don't wish for rings before Soko, you'll have 4 guranteed there... If you  
have enough food to reach Soko, food should not be such a big trouble  
afterwards. Ring of SD is nice but I won't burn a wish on it (except as a  
Vampire, of course).

You'll probably find enough scrolls of genocide to wipe out h and L  
without too many trouble. Wishing for them might be useful, but not that  
much, imho.

A blessed figurine of a Solar is always funny, but of course you'll want  
to have a magic whistle before that...

So, I'll probably go for :
Deep DSM (other drain resistance took out amulet and you may find amulet  
of reflection in Soko).
Cloak of MR.
Whisperfeet.
[do Soko]
amulet of reflection/wallet of Perseus (depending on Soko outcome).

The 2 other slots are more open, imho.

